{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"I’ve been building iOS apps for over a decade, first in Turkey and now in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Germany. The work I care about most is the part users never see: clean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"architecture, tests you can trust, and release tooling that lets a small team"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ship often. It’s unglamorous. It’s also what makes release day boring, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the goal."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Right now that means 70+ public transport apps on one Swift codebase at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"ioki","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", part of a mobility platform that has served nearly 10 million"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passengers. Before that I worked on messaging ("},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"BiP","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", 3.5M monthly users),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"banking ("},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"QNB Finansbank","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), live events at "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cisco","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", where we shipped 100+"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"branded apps from one codebase, and public transport at "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Kentkart","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When I led a team at Ecospend, I did the groundwork for each new feature","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"myself: the interfaces, the services and the test cases it had to pass. Then","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"someone on the team built the rest.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This site is where I keep my CV and write about the tools I use. The pages are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named like a release: the changelog is my work history, the dependencies are my","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stack, and the patch notes are articles.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Currently","anchor":"Currently"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Senior iOS Developer at ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ioki","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" in Frankfurt, working on ticketing,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real-time ride tracking and release tooling.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Writing about iOS tooling. The latest pieces cover a DocC documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pipeline, writing your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" operator, and turning DocC into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a personal site.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Get in touch","level":3,"anchor":"Get-in-touch","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/haydar-karkin\/"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/haydarKarkin","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ReleaseNotes\/documentation\/ReleaseNotes\/Experience"],"title":"Changelog","abstract":[{"text":"Work history: what shipped, w